{"text": "OFFICE OF THE GOVERNOR\nApril 24, 2017\nVia Electronic Mail\n\nMr. Tom Nash\n36186-06490635@requests.muckrock.com\n\nRE: Public Records Act Request\n\nDear Mr. Nash:\n\nThis letter responds to your correspondence received on April 17, 2017 requesting all\nletters, emails, or memos relating to the parole of Hampig \u201cHarry\u201d Sassounian sent or received\nby the Governor\u2019s Office.\n\nThe records responsive to your request are all exempt from disclosure. (See Gov. Code,\n\u00a7 6254, subd. (f) [exempting investigative and security records conducted for correctional\npurposes]; \u00a7 6254, subd. (/) [exempting \u201c[c]orrespondence of and to the Governor or employees\nof the Governor\u2019s office,\u201d or records in the custody of or maintained by the Governor\u2019s Legal\nAffairs Secretary]; Gov. Code, \u00a7 6254, subd. (k) [exempting records subject to the attorney-\nclient privilege]; Gov. Code, \u00a7 6255; Cal. First Amend. Coalition v. Super. Ct. (1998) 67\nCal.App.4th 159; Times Mirror Co. v. Super. Ct. (1991) 53 Cal.3d 1325 [exempting records that\nreveal the deliberative process of the Governor or his staff].)\n\nSincerely,\n\nREIR. ONISHI\nDeputy Legal Affairs Secretary\n\nGOVERNOR EDMUND G. BROWN JR. * SACRAMENTO, CALIFORNIA 95814 * (916) 445-2841",
